{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe Gerrit Verify matrix runs the same default-tier marker selection on Ubuntu Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13. Every cell currently enables pytest-cov and independently enforces the same repository-wide fail-under floor. All three cells remain necessary for supported-Python behavioral and contractual compatibility, but tracing identical source on three cells adds runner occupancy without a distinct verdict. Production code has no sys.version_info or sys.version branches. The closed ropeable-hydrated-siskin ticket established the accepted precedent of retaining platform tests while collecting coverage only on a primary cell. Ubuntu Python 3.13 is the primary cell because it is the newest stable supported interpreter already paired with the sole macOS compatibility cell; retaining the gate there keeps the coverage verdict on the primary runtime while 3.11 and 3.12 remain behavioral-compatibility legs.\n\n## Plan\n- Measure instrumentation cost on the same checkout and host with identical tests/unit selection and worker count: one untimed warm-up, then A-B-B-A-A-B where A includes the production coverage flags and B omits only those flags. Report local_delta = median(A elapsed) - median(B elapsed).\n- Record this change own pre-merge Verify run id, the Python 3.11 and 3.12 default-suite step durations, and the post-merge comparison formula on this ticket before close. The umbrella inedible-subsimious-brahmancow owns the same-session post-merge observation because GitHub resolves the reusable workflow from main during pre-merge workflow_dispatch. The umbrella remains open until it records the first post-merge run, each changed-cell delta = pre-merge step duration - post-merge step duration, and the sum of only Python 3.11 and 3.12 deltas as runner-seconds freed. Python 3.13 and macOS are unchanged controls. The report must label a one-run comparison as noisy and must not call summed parallel time critical-path wall time.\n- Survey Django, NumPy, and SciPy current workflows and record each topology and any documented rationale as found. Consensus passes only if at least two selectively collect coverage on a primary or dedicated configuration while broader compatibility jobs run uninstrumented and none documents rejecting that practice for coverage or reliability. If the threshold fails, stop before Phase 2 and summarize the contrary evidence for the operator.\n- Extend tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py with a workflow contract that expands the declared matrix. Prove all four cells retain both default and integration pytest tiers. Prove exactly Ubuntu Python 3.13 receives both coverage flags and the other three cells receive neither.\n- Encode the condition with the non-empty coverage flag string in the truthy and-slot and the empty string only in the final or-slot. This explicitly avoids the GitHub Actions empty-string-falsy trap recorded on ropeable-hydrated-siskin. Defect-seed the prior all-Ubuntu condition and a zero-coverage condition; each must make the held-out contract RED before restoring GREEN.\n- Update the coverage rationale comment in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml and the canonical topology in docs/coverage.md so both state that Ubuntu Python 3.13 alone collects branch coverage and enforces fail-under.\n- Run focused workflow tests, lint, and typecheck; land through Gerrit. Back-out is a Gerrit revert restoring the prior all-Ubuntu coverage condition and three-cell documentation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The A-B-B-A-A-B experiment reports raw elapsed samples.\n- [ ] The experiment reports local_delta using the stated median formula.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.11 retains the default-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.11 retains the integration-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.12 retains the default-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.12 retains the integration-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.13 retains the default-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.13 retains the integration-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] macOS Python 3.13 retains the default-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] macOS Python 3.13 retains the integration-tier pytest step.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.13 collects branch coverage.\n- [ ] Ubuntu Python 3.13 enforces the unchanged fail-under threshold.\n- [ ] No other matrix cell receives a coverage flag.\n- [ ] The workflow contract is observed RED with the prior all-Ubuntu coverage condition.\n- [ ] The workflow contract is observed RED when no cell receives coverage.\n- [ ] The survey records a current workflow URL and topology for each named project.\n- [ ] The survey records any documented rejection found.\n- [ ] The consensus decision applies the stated threshold to the recorded findings.\n- [ ] Tracker history cites ropeable-hydrated-siskin and any prior rejection found.\n- [ ] The workflow rationale comment describes the one-cell coverage topology.\n- [ ] docs/coverage.md describes the one-cell coverage topology.\n- [ ] Focused tests pass.\n- [ ] Lint passes.\n- [ ] Typecheck passes.\n- [ ] Gerrit LLM-Review is +1 with zero unresolved comments.\n- [ ] Gerrit Verified is +1 before merge.\n- [ ] The pre-merge baseline run id and raw 3.11/3.12 default-suite step durations are recorded before close.\n- [ ] The post-merge observation is explicitly tracked on inedible-subsimious-brahmancow.\n- [ ] Back-out is documented as a Gerrit revert restoring the prior condition and topology text."}},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786703450146138001,"uuid":"ec3e2b4c-2b06-4b27-b08d-7633a0bc312f"}